# Typed-only variadics (no ...rest fallback) produce an exhaustiveness warning.
# The type checker warns that non-String/Int args would fail at runtime.
# Functions with only typed buckets intentionally restrict arg types.
[f: [fn [let ...strings@String ...nums@Int] [head strings]]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(strings, nums)})

=== warn
non-exhaustive variadic type dispatch: typed buckets cover [or Integer String] but no fallback (...rest) handles other types — add ...rest for a wildcard bucket
